{
  "case_id": "2009-09-223",
  "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:56 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So why can't the Pullman doctrine or the Burford doctrine, abstention doctrines, be enough to counsel Federal abstention in this case? Why do we have to create another exception to Hibbs and not go to another established abstention doctrine?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Ohio",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MIZER: Well, to be frank, Your Honor, the State of Ohio joined an amicus brief urging the opposite outcome in Hibbs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But I have no idea -- why I am asking the question is I have no idea or little idea of the underlying State law merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fitch",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0001-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there are businesses all over the country and there's Federal tax law, too. And suddenly people begin to think: Hey, this is a terrific idea; I am going to go through my competitor's tax returns and I will discover taxes they should have paid but didn't, and all of a sudden we will face a lot of lawsuits challenging other people's taxes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you know of any case where a benefit that A enjoys is taken away from A in a suit where A is not a party?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State's motion to dismiss was under -- under 12(b)(1), which is a motion to dismiss for lack of subject matter jurisdiction, and that was granted by the court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fitch",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But, Your Honor, the point we are making is that some court somewhere has to make the decision whether this exemption violates the dormant Commerce Clause in the equal protection case. And it was our judgment that the best forum for that was in Federal court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you -- do you recognize that comity is broader than the Tax Injunction Act, and if it is, how do you justify your argument that would essentially limit the comity doctrine to the contours of the Tax Injunction Act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fitch",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "in Coors, is what the Sixth Circuit says is that comity extends broader than the TIA. What they point to repeatedly is Fair Assessment, because Fair Assessment got damages and it was on a comity basis that the Court held in Fair Assessment that you couldn't get around your own liability by bringing a damage claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I understand your point about regulation and nonregulation, but -- but your competitors are subject to a different taxing regime than you are; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Mizer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "419669bb092d1682221dbdfe72991eeeb401e5a6f44395cff5cda4cd6b6c38f9",
      "evidence_id": "ev-419669bb092d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If we are talking about the Tax Injunction Act, Grace Brethren holds that even a declaration of unconstitutionality is problematic under the Tax Injunction Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-09-223",
      "confidence": 0.0,
